-- title:
--   One relative allocation bound supplies every wanted-reporting buffer
-- statement:
--   Fix machine limits and natural reporting parameters $h,J,K,N,N_B,N_C,V$, with allocation base $z$. Let $C_{\mathrm{want}}$ be the defined sum of wanted-layout storage, numerical allowance, and scratch allowance. If
--
--   $$
--   z+C_{\mathrm{want}}(h,J,K,N,N_B,N_C,V)\le\mathrm{space},
--   $$
--
--   then all components of the wanted-buffer specification fit in space: the work pointer plus the numerical allowance, terminal-reporter storage, query workspace, decoder workspace, and the $512h+1$ packing cells. The bound also covers $J+512h+\operatorname{groupSize}(h)+\operatorname{sourceCut}(h,J)$ and every value stored in the constructed layout header.
--
--   This consolidates the reporting buffer checks into one bound relative to the caller's allocation base.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsWanted.lean#L87-L112

